BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 596.16 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 575.37 Td (Releases BERT models further pre-trained on MIMIC-III clinical notes, one on all notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 560.88 Td (and one on discharge summaries only, and shows gains over general-domain and biomedical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 546.39 Td (BERT on several clinical NLP tasks, though not on de-identification.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 511.83 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 491.04 Td (Neural language models have become the default tool for a wide range of text) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 476.55 Td (understanding problems. This question has become central as models are deployed on longer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 462.06 Td (and more heterogeneous inputs, and as practitioners weigh accuracy against cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 441.27 Td (Clinical notes differ from general-domain text in vocabulary, abbreviation density, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 426.78 Td (document length; a typical discharge summary in MIMIC-III exceeds 1,500 word pieces, far) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 412.29 Td (beyond the 512-token window of standard encoders.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 377.73 Td (2 Related Work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 356.94 Td (Prior work spans architectural changes to the attention mechanism, training objectives) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 342.45 Td (tailored to the target domain, and evaluation suites that probe robustness. We review the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 327.96 Td (most closely related approaches and highlight where our assumptions differ.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 293.40 Td (3 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 272.61 Td (We describe the model architecture, the training objective and the optimization schedule,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 258.12 Td (and note where our choices depart from common practice. We stratify performance by note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 243.63 Td (type \(discharge summary, radiology, nursing\) and by patient subgroups to assess whether) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 229.14 Td (gains are uniform across the population.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0 g 72 194.58 Td (4 Experiments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 173.79 Td (All data were accessed under the PhysioNet credentialed data use agreement. Protected) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 159.30 Td (health information had been removed by the dataset curators prior to release, and no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 144.81 Td (attempt was made to re-identify patients.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 124.02 Td (Results are reported as the mean over five random seeds with standard deviations in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 109.53 Td (parentheses. Statistical significance is assessed with a paired bootstrap test at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0 g 72 95.04 Td (0.05 level.) Tj ET
